   "id": 57,
   "plugin": "Core",
   "model": "Notes",
   "data": {
    "text": "COMEDY\nPatch any CV (0 to 10 V) into a jack. 0 V is the item's From setting, 10 V its To.\n\nCV-CC 1: MIDI channel 6, CC 17 to 32\n   1 Kind of joke\n   2 What the joke is about\n   3 Pause before the punchline\n   4 Escalation\n   5 Absurdity\n   6 Deadpan to broad\n   7 Cringe\n   8 Setup and payoff\n   9 Scenes from setup to payoff\n  10 Laughs per minute\n  11 Who carries the joke\n  12 Reaction to the joke\n  13 Running gag\n  14 Callback\n  15 Rule of three\n  16 Physical comedy\nCV-CC 2: MIDI channel 6, CC 33 to 48\n   1 Wordplay\n   2 Misdirection\n   3 Irony\n   4 Understatement\n   5 Fish out of water\n   6 Visual gag\n   7 Subversion\n   8 Comic edit\n   9 Comic sound\n  10 Comic flaw\n  11 Comic premise\n  12 The topper\n  13 Oddly specific\n  14 Talking to the camera\n  15 Exaggeration\n  16 Humiliation\nCV-CC 3: MIDI channel 6, CC 49 to 64\n   1 The lie that grows\n   2 Misunderstanding\n   3 Cutaway gag\n   4 suite: Comedy lens\n   5 suite: Where the laugh comes from\n   6 suite: Deadpan\n   7 suite: Slapstick\n   8 suite: Mockumentary\n   9 suite: Screwball\n  10 suite: Cringe comedy\n  11 suite: Absurdist\n  12 suite: Dark comedy\n  13 suite: Rom-com banter\n  14 suite: Snowball disaster\n  15 suite: Pull-back reveal\n  16 suite: Smash cut contradiction\nCV-CC 4: MIDI channel 6, CC 65 to 80\n   1 suite: Background gags\n   2 suite: Farce\n   3 suite: The topper\n   4 suite: Punching up\n   5 suite: The aside\n   6 suite: Oddly specific world\n   7 suite: Blind to their flaw\n   8 suite: The cutaway that contradicts\n   9 suite: Bigger than life\n  10 pair: When a joke's setup is planted, the payoff lands\n  11 pair: When the escalation rises, the absurdity rises\n  12 pair: When the pause before the punchline grows, laughs per minute drop but each lands harder\n  13 pair: After a big joke, cut to a reaction\n  14 pair: Two of a pattern, then the break\n  15 pair: \"I'll never\", then they do\n  16 pair: After a cringe, a pointed silence\nCV-CC 5: MIDI channel 6, CC 81 to 96\n   1 pair: As trouble escalates, the frame widens\n   2 pair: A running gag returns, bigger\n   3 pair: A joke line returns in a tender moment\n   4 pair: Something absurd, nobody reacts\n   5 pair: Misdirection pays off with a pull-back\n   6 pair: After tension, a laugh breaks it\n   7 pair: When a joke lands, a topper follows\n   8 pair: When a lie wobbles, a bigger lie covers it\n   9 pair: When the lie collapses, someone is humiliated\n  10 pair: When a misunderstanding deepens, the chaos grows\n  11 pair: When someone is humiliated in front of others, the cringe rises\n  12 pair: When a blind flaw grows, the character is set back\n  13 pair: When a character talks to us, the others react a beat late\n  14 pair: An oddly specific detail comes back later\n  15 pairs: Joke machine\n  16 pairs: Long-game comedy\nCV-CC 6: MIDI channel 6, CC 97 to 101\n   1 pairs: Comic reversals\n   2 pairs: The camera sells the joke\n   3 pairs: The farce engine\n   4 pairs: Stacking laughs\n   5 pairs: Comedy of a flaw"
